Modifications, 2026-11-17:
The simulation loader converts the released skeleton STL from millimetres to
metres, shares coincident vertices, and represents it as a fixed collision mesh.
The diagnostics add rigid hollow coupons and a discrete compliant hollow tube
using the published tube sizes. The compliant tube starts on a centerline
measured from the editable CAD's evaluated index-extension clearance cutter.
The loader partitions the released index finger and flexible inserts by mesh
connectivity while preserving all original triangles and source coordinates.
These are simulation adaptations, not manufacturer-validated repair procedures.
New hardware-derived simulation source in this folder is CERN-OHL-S-2.0.
The full licence is provided in LICENSE-HARDWARE.txt.

mechkit.py is the repository's shared mechanism helper, copied from the version
credited to tasks/heat-shrink-lug/mechkit.py. Its original provenance is retained.
Local changes increase geometry output precision and reduce collision offsets
for this small-scale diagnostic. It is an external simulation-tool component,
not a claim to authorship of the hardware design.

Use of the hardware reference's name is solely for source attribution and does
not imply endorsement. No source CAD archive is embedded in this folder.

Additional diagnostic adaptations, 2026-11-17:
The initial route is optionally smoothed between the source endpoint guides.
An eight-segment approximation and carrier-mass redistribution compare contact
stability. Redistribution preserves locked-cell mass moments within serialized
precision but changes internal hinge inertia; no exact dynamic equivalence or
validated hardware behavior is claimed. No original CAD triangles are changed.
